Adaptations for FastLLM: independent request descriptors, paged KV, existing
FP8 rounding and scale order, attention sinks, workspace ownership and admission.
Full-layer projection helpers derive from attn_common/rows_gemv_mma.cuh.
The full-layer adapter uses FastLLM normalization, RoPE/cache semantics,
TP mailbox transport and residual rounding. Its compact QK/PV fragments and
distributed split combine adapt qk_eight_heads, pv_eight_heads and compute_attention
from attn_dsa/attn_dsa_body.cuh. The original attention path remains available.

The BF16 dense verification adapter in
src/devices/cuda/moe/fastllm-shared-flex-dense-sm103.cuh adapts normalize_rows,
project_rows_mma and checkpoint_bf16's SwiGLU/projection geometry from the same
pinned NaiveRT commit. FastLLM modifications preserve its BF16 materialization
boundaries, runtime row tails/chunking, existing weight/workspace ownership,
collective admission and rank-ordered TP transport. The original license and
attribution apply to these derived fragments as well.
